WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.159 --> 00:00:01.240
(audience cheers)
- We've hit the moment

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:03.580
when I get to share with you
something totally amazing

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:05.300
that you may have missed
on your social feeds.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.500
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:07.424 --> 00:00:09.630
(upbeat music)
(audience cheers)

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:12.330
Looking for work as a
mom isn't always easy.

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:14.270
Sometimes there's no
one to watch the kiddos

00:00:14.270 --> 00:00:16.000
when you're brought in for an interview.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.130
One mama came up with a creative
way to tackle that dilemma.

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:23.320
She brought her son Milo
along but it's how she did it,

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:26.559
that's attracted so much attention. Watch.

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:29.142
(upbeat music)

00:00:30.367 --> 00:00:32.950
(upbeat music)

00:00:35.077 --> 00:00:38.494
(upbeat music continues)

00:00:41.717 --> 00:00:43.240
(audience claps)

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:46.010
I mean, I would hire her like on the spot.

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:47.093
That's amazing.

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:48.780
That's right.

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:49.720
Just like his mom Maggie,

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:51.930
Milo was dressed in proper work attire.

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:55.630
He had his resume, all set and
he walked in with confidence.

00:00:55.630 --> 00:00:58.550
We have Maggie and Milo
on the line right now.

00:00:58.550 --> 00:00:59.383
What's up?

00:00:59.383 --> 00:01:01.490
(audience cheers)

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:02.891
(audience cheers)
- Hi.

00:01:02.891 --> 00:01:04.560
(audience claps)
- Ah!

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.520
Oh man, a little one in a little suit

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:07.960
is never not adorable.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:11.180
So were you hesitant
to take Milo with you?

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:12.283
- You know what Kelly

00:01:12.283 --> 00:01:14.650
I have been a national sales
trainer with a company.

00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:16.910
It was about 13 years when
I was with the company,

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:18.390
I was laid off.

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:19.980
Sorry, you know how this is.

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:21.100
- Yes, absolutely let him run.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:24.660
- I was laid off during my pregnancy leave

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:29.660
and so when I finally had
an opportunity to interview

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:31.600
with the company and they invited me back

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:33.765
for a second interview, I was excited,

00:01:33.765 --> 00:01:37.270
but I had to let them know
that I didn't have childcare.

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:39.900
And they replied by letting me know

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:41.870
that they were family friendly.

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:46.040
And so I was excited and gladly accepted.

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:48.730
And then let them know that I would have

00:01:48.730 --> 00:01:50.600
my little interview ready also.

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:52.370
So I dressed him up in a little suit

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:54.640
and made him a little resume

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:56.570
and just to have fun with it.

00:01:56.570 --> 00:01:57.930
- Oh my god. It's amazing.

00:01:57.930 --> 00:01:59.520
So how did the interview go?

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:00.440
- It was amazing.

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:03.900
So when I went in, it was
completely not traditional.

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:05.860
As you might imagine,

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:07.610
he ate the owners pickle

00:02:07.610 --> 00:02:10.730
and it was a great experience.
(laughs)

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:12.690
I ultimately declined the position.

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:15.490
It just wasn't the right fit
for me, now I'm consulting,

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:20.170
but it led to a great
conversation worldwide

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:22.110
about the childcare crisis.

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:25.350
And it gave me a platform
to talk about how

00:02:25.350 --> 00:02:27.060
this is impacting parents like me.

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:29.730
And so many people responded to my Tiktok

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:31.840
and it was like we created
this mini community.

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:33.880
It was amazing.

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:37.100
Even Senator Elizabeth
Warren shared my Tiktok

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:40.570
and I'm excited to share
with you that next year

00:02:40.570 --> 00:02:43.060
I will get to go to Washington DC.

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:47.030
And I actually get to talk to
a group of about 300 people

00:02:47.030 --> 00:02:48.710
sharing my experience to advocate

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:51.457
for the childcare crisis in the US.

00:02:51.457 --> 00:02:52.383
(audience cheers)
- That's amazing.

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:55.280
Wow,
(audience claps)

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:57.850
that's an amazing opportunity
that you're honestly

00:02:57.850 --> 00:02:59.770
gonna help out a lot of parents out there

00:02:59.770 --> 00:03:01.140
that have a hard time finding childcare.

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:02.770
It's hard to keep a job

00:03:02.770 --> 00:03:05.680
and keep that balance
alive with your family.

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:06.990
Well, thank you so much, Maggie.

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:08.310
And thank you Milo!

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:09.143
(audience cheers)

00:03:09.143 --> 00:03:11.260
We're liking your post right now.

00:03:11.260 --> 00:03:12.320
(audience claps)

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:14.260
Well, that's not all,
our season long partner,

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.100
Pilot Pen, makers of FriXion,

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:18.500
the go-to erasable pen of
the Kelly Clarkson show

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:20.470
want to celebrate those
creating fearlessly,

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:21.720
just like you ma'am.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:23.440
So they're gonna give you a 1000 dollars.

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:25.073
How's that sound?
(audience cheers)

00:03:25.073 --> 00:03:27.525
(audience cheers)
- Oh my gosh, thank you Kelly.

00:03:27.525 --> 00:03:28.509
Thank you.

00:03:28.509 --> 00:03:30.310
[Kelly] No, absolutely.

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:32.930
And good luck going to DC that's awesome.

